Hi,

MissingPercentage is a metric that is peptide specific for a particular run.  For example, in this table below, run 1 for peptide ATDVIVPEEGELR has a 0% missingPercentage because it has measurements on all 6 features, but run 2 has a 33% missingPercentage for peptide ATDVIVPEEGELR because it has measurements on only 4 of 6 features.

Feature      |         Run          |       MissingPercentage
ATDVIVPEEGELR_2_y6 | 1 | 0%
ATDVIVPEEGELR_2_y7 | 1 | 0%
ATDVIVPEEGELR_2_y8 | 1 | 0%
ATDVIVPEEGELR_2_y9 | 1 | 0%
ATDVIVPEEGELR_2_y10 | 1 | 0%
ATDVIVPEEGELR_2_y11 | 1 | 0%
ATDVIVPEEGELR_2_y6 | 2 | 33%
ATDVIVPEEGELR_2_y9 | 2 | 33%
ATDVIVPEEGELR_2_y10 | 2 | 33%
ATDVIVPEEGELR_2_y11 | 2 | 33%

This MissingPercentage can indicate that certain MS runs have less missing values for particular peptides than others.

Thanks,
Tony

